  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 20-layer HfO2/SiO2 alternating multilayer stack on fused silica substrate for solar-blind UV filter application. Wavelength bands: 255-280 nm (high transmittance target), 300-700 nm (suppressed transmittance), 700-1100 nm (suppressed transmittance). Air incidence, normal angle, unpolarized. Initialize thicknesses from Round 1 baseline: [32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17, 32.62, 45.17] nm. Apply hard clip bounds of ±2.5 nm per layer during optimization. Use multi-start gradient-based local optimizer with 10 random starts within bounds. Material registry resolves HfO2 and SiO2 optical constants. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, thicknesses_nm for all valid candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 255-280 nm, 300-700 nm, 700-1100 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 255–280 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Transmittance in 300–700 nm; Transmittance in 700–1100 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum 30 layers; No metal layers; Only conventional depositable inorganic dielectric materials.",
